Read AGENTS.md before editing. It is the canonical instruction set.

Architecture, in one paragraph: routes in src/app are thin and call a module
surface; features live in src/modules with fixed layer directories (actions,
services, repositories, providers, mappers, policies, schemas, helpers, types,
constants, components, containers, hooks); vendors are wrapped one-per-directory
in src/packages; src/shared is generic. Cross-module imports go through a
declared surface file, never into another module's directories.

Hard rules, all lint-enforced:
- Every dashboard repository call takes an ownerId in the WHERE clause.
- Tenant-free reads carry an Unscoped suffix and are confined to the public path.
- Stored JSON is parsed through portfolioDocumentSchema, never cast.
- The public render path imports no AI, ingestion, editor, storage or auth code.
- No eslint-disable comments; exceptions live in eslint/exceptions.config.mjs.
- No raw className outside the design system; no literal user-facing strings.
- process.env only inside src/packages/env.
- No non-null assertions.

Testing: pure logic is held at 100% coverage, everything unit-tested at 95%.
Repositories, actions, providers and services are covered by the Playwright
suite against a real database, not by mocks.

Never weaken a gate to make it pass.

Communication (rules/08-communication-style.md): 1-5 short lines by default.
Name the exact file, error, count or blocker. A blocker starts with "Blocked:".
"Done." carries its proof. No filler openers. Never claim background work that
is not actually running.

Executive function (rules/09-executive-function.md): state objective,
Definition of Done and scope before deep reasoning. Classify discoveries;
only BLOCKER/REQUIRED may interrupt the current task. Respect the nesting,
retry and critic budgets. Stop when done. Recover from a stall with
skills/recover-from-a-loop.md.
